    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of brush and shrub cover in the immediate vicinity of the structure would meaningfully improve defensible space and reduce fuel continuity near the building. Brush growing adjacent to the structure should be thinned or cleared to create separation between combustible vegetation and the building envelope, which may reduce structure exposure and support suppression operations if fire approaches. Along the long driveway, managing vegetation to maintain adequate clearance on both sides would support firefighter access and improve conditions for emergency ingress and egress. Reducing connections between dense shrub patches across the property could interrupt fuel continuity and limit the opportunity for fire to spread toward improvements. The existing water feature represents a valuable on-site resource and maintaining it in operable condition could support suppression efforts. Continued vegetation management within the immediate structure perimeter, combined with ongoing attention to brush density in the broader surrounding area, would support long-term wildfire resilience for this property."
